00:04:31.007 --> 00:04:32.090
VICTOR SALMONS: All right.

00:04:32.090 --> 00:04:33.975
Good afternoon, folks.

00:04:33.975 --> 00:04:36.100
It's really a pleasure to
be here and talk with you

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:38.470
about Zebra Technologies.

00:04:38.470 --> 00:04:42.370
We're going to talk
about thermal printers

00:04:42.370 --> 00:04:46.700
and we're going to talk about
our partnership with MicroEJ.

00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:49.510
So let's start with printers.

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:52.090
Printers, they're
mission critical devices

00:04:52.090 --> 00:04:54.800
that live in our
customers' environments.

00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:59.440
We need to deliver
labels, receipts, cards

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:00.940
when the customers want it.

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:04.560
I mean, these are real
time embedded devices.

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:08.650
They're electromechanical,
really complex devices.

00:05:08.650 --> 00:05:10.150
And they are constrained.

00:05:10.150 --> 00:05:12.790
We know constrained devices
in the embedded world.

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:16.290
They're constrained
by their design,

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:18.060
they're constrained
by the cost--

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:22.770
we're always trading those
off-- constrained by lifecycle.

00:05:22.770 --> 00:05:25.997
We're also constrained by
that real time component.

00:05:25.997 --> 00:05:28.080
And what comes to mind is
a use case that we have.

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:32.190
We print at 12 inches per
second and 400 microseconds

00:05:32.190 --> 00:05:36.400
is really, really
critical in that use case.

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:41.000
So think about-- we have to get
data through the system, format

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:46.090
bitmaps, make bitmaps,
get them into a printhead,

00:05:46.090 --> 00:05:49.490
and at 12 inches per
second we're pumping 2,400

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:52.540
dots an eighth of a millimeter.

00:05:52.540 --> 00:05:55.340
2,400 dots an eighth
of a millimeter

00:05:55.340 --> 00:05:59.900
every 400 microseconds, that's
that real time constraint

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:02.090
that we have to
live under in order

00:06:02.090 --> 00:06:04.880
to deliver on those mission
critical applications

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:07.620
for our customers.

00:06:07.620 --> 00:06:09.840
But in this day and age,
we need to go faster.

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:13.710
All that real time stuff takes
us time to develop to make sure

00:06:13.710 --> 00:06:15.000
we get it right--

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:17.950
make sure we get it
right every single time.

00:06:17.950 --> 00:06:19.680
So imagine in this
day and age where

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:21.530
things are moving so quickly--

00:06:21.530 --> 00:06:25.260
IoT is moving, use
cases are changing--

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:31.310
imagine if we could have a
way to go faster, and develop

00:06:31.310 --> 00:06:35.420
applications on top of that real
time, and keep them separated--

00:06:35.420 --> 00:06:39.350
keep them managed, so that
we're delivering that real time,

00:06:39.350 --> 00:06:44.030
but we're able to go faster
and make those applications.

00:06:44.030 --> 00:06:49.220
I think we have solved that
with our MicroEJ partnership.

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:51.830
So I'm going to tease you
with that a little bit

00:06:51.830 --> 00:06:53.630
and talk about it in
a minute, but first I

00:06:53.630 --> 00:06:56.510
want to talk about
Zebra Technologies.

00:06:56.510 --> 00:07:00.770
You see Zebra Technologies every
day in your day-to-day life.

00:07:00.770 --> 00:07:02.930
We're right there
in front of you.

00:07:02.930 --> 00:07:07.720
You see us in retail helping
you to purchase that shirt

00:07:07.720 --> 00:07:10.720
or your favorite dress.

00:07:10.720 --> 00:07:14.200
You see us with that delivery
driver getting that package

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:17.170
to your doorstep
quickly and reliably.

00:07:17.170 --> 00:07:20.800
You see us in health
care, matching patients

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:25.480
with critical medications.

00:07:25.480 --> 00:07:29.770
When your car is returned
through that rental car,

00:07:29.770 --> 00:07:32.110
we're there to get
you fast through it

00:07:32.110 --> 00:07:33.730
and get you to your terminal.

00:07:33.730 --> 00:07:37.760
And, last but not least,
you see us in the NFL.

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:42.920
That's right, we're tracking and
tracing players in real time.

00:07:42.920 --> 00:07:44.425
That's Zebra.

00:07:44.425 --> 00:07:45.800
We're right there
in front of you

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:48.320
and I'll just give you
a little bit of history.

00:07:48.320 --> 00:07:53.580
Zebra's celebrating 50 years as
a technology company this year.

00:07:53.580 --> 00:07:55.700
We've been at it for 50 years.

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:58.880
I heard recently that most
